## Advisory — Radical Innovation

Not applied to the plan; restated from the prior run since it remains unaddressed and still the most leveraged change available here. **Make the cache validate cheaply instead of expiring never.** Have `discoverThemes` (or a new `discoveryRoots(opts)`) report the roots it walked; `ThemeCache` records those roots' `fs.statSync().mtimeMs` at scan completion and, on `load`, re-stats them (single-digit ms) before deciding whether to serve the cached list as-is or kick a refresh. This gets closer to "serve immediately, refresh when something actually changed" without the per-command full rescan the creative rejected, and without `fs.watch`, a worker, or persistence — it only closes the gap for added/removed/renamed files, not in-place edits, so the operator should judge whether that partial coverage is worth the extra `signature()` helper versus the current "reload the window" answer.
